{
  "family": "monochromatic-copy",
  "canonical_name": "Hypergraph.foundations.hypergraph_copies.hg_mono_copy",
  "canonical_short_name": "hg_mono_copy",
  "relation": "Monochromatic copy of a supplied pattern: for E : {set {set T}} and a colouring col : {set U} -> C of ALL subsets of a finite host U, some colour c and some injection f : T -> U of the whole pattern carrier (isolated vertices included) give col (f @: e) = c for every member e. For an eqType palette it is containment (hg_containsb) of the pattern in one colour class [set e | col e == c]. No uniformity, rank, nonempty family/carrier, positive palette or no-isolated premise; a colouring into the empty palette I_0 cannot exist (set0), so q = 0 forcing stays vacuous as written. Forcing, Ramsey minimality, C8 constancy on a supplied set and the Extremal graph copies (X4, XE1, edge_colourings.mono_copy) are separate.",
  "baseline_commit": "598d668fa9225c8271852c856ce3990c7fa7890e",
