  "summary": [
    "D4 turns X108/X117 (bool) and X119 (I_q) monochromatic_copy into aliases of the new public Hypergraph.foundations.hypergraph_copies.hg_mono_copy: one colour, one whole-carrier injection, every member mapped by f @: e to a host set of that colour; hg_mono_copyP is the colour-class bridge to hg_containsb. The bool aliases are the same term, so x117_monochromatic_copyE stays a conversion.",
    "Frozen at the D3 pin: 3 sources, 5 chains (two-colour and q-colour forcing, both Ramsey predicates with forcing and minimality) and 3 complete current rows (3 new whole iff, all conversions). The complete histories are D3's existing X108ImageOriginal, X119ImageOriginal and complete X117ImageLegacy rows, bound at 9e03072 with D3's certificates (3 reused whole iff).",
    "The D3 images and copy/forcing/Ramsey chains and the D1/A10 support reached by those rows are listed in the historical role. Three proof lines of D3's copy certificates were adapted (statements unchanged) because the live copies now unfold to f @: e.",
    "Statuses, legs, docs, the X119 no-isolated guard, the opaque x119_sqrt_ex witness and the q = 0 forcing behaviour are unchanged. Public client: hypergraph-theory/theories/examples/monochromatic_copies.v."
  ],
  "kernel_evidence": "Exact types/implicit status of the sources and API, the six whole iff, all old declarations against 598d668, the 21 actual consumers, Print Assumptions, About-resolved Print All Dependencies closures and the sqrt witness, through the pinned image. /srv/graph-theory-rocq/coordination/evidence/D4-by-lancelot/ (outside the repository)",
